  "summary": "Simulation-validated EFT, n(z), baryonification and lens-multipole studies target biases that would limit DESI, Euclid, SKA and time-delay cosmology.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is validating the theory and nuisance models that sit between large-scale-structure observables and cosmological parameters. For Lyman-alpha tracers, the methods are effective field theory approaches. One paper tests a minimal tree-level EFT on simulated 21 cm, Lyα, and cross-power spectra at z=2.4–4.2 to constrain HI and Lyα biases. Another validates an EFT full-shape analysis of the Lyα power spectrum and bispectrum on AbacusSummit mocks at z=2.5 for DESI. Nuisance modeling is also addressed. On-the-fly Gaussian Process reconstruction of n(z) for Euclid-like 3×2pt analyses finds that redshift-distribution systematics can bias w0wa. Baryonification produces tSZ Compton-y maps from dark-matter-only lightcones. IllustrisTNG ellipticals show that multipole mass terms bias time-delay H0 inference by 1–6%. Alongside this, observational and new-physics probes include genus topology of SDSS galaxies against HR4 simulations, boosted dark matter signatures forecast for SKA1-Low, and a GR test using galaxy cluster clustering from the DESI Legacy Imaging Surveys.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-opus-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-18"
}
